# b5-innsbruck-quit: the battle of session 9 (Innsbruck, 1805), played by the Allies, who
# defend. At the first order the player takes Intell, then quits with F10 at the map cursor.
# F10 writes no OUTCOME.&&& (TODO.md, "The game"), so the run must write none, as DOS did.
# The battle's BATTLE.$$$ is b5-innsbruck-quit.battle.
# seed 1 (NAP_SEED)

# A TICK of a second or more: any key ends it. A "hit a key" pause: a space.
rule 3 key f12
rule 1 key space
play until 5
# shot first-order
state
text i
play until 6
# shot intell
state
key f10
# F10 ends the program by the SYSTEM of NAPOLEON.BAS, after scriptend("Q").
play until 7:Q
# shot result
state
key f12
